@Al  in Pittsburgh

That's not what unitary executive theory is. It means that all executive power flows through the president and any executive agency serves at the directive of the president.

Historically, we've had a concept of an independent justice department, for example. Unitary executive theory states that the president can direct and suspend prosecutions the same way he can direct any other executive agency

